  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Load Kea or Tecmag CPMG/T1Sat/SSE-T2 echo data in the browser (Pyodide), inspect the echoes, fit multi-exponential and inverse-Laplace models to the decay (overall or per depth position z), add MCMC/bootstrap uncertainty, and export tables, figures, a report and provenance. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
